## TRIAGE RESULTS

### Finding 1: CBS Proxy WebSocket — Anonymous IDOR/BOLA (`cbs-proxy.api.live-manager.de`)

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — `*.live-manager.de` in scope; `cbs-proxy.api.live-manager.de` resolves to 185.158.98.53 (in-scope /22) |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — public, zero credentials, anonymous WS upgrade returns HTTP 101 |
| Q3 Impact | YES — cross-tenant exposure of customer business-system call/debug streams (PII/voice) |
| Q4 Provable | YES — read-only WS handshake confirmed (101 + CONNECT CBS100/190/200 + READY for cid=1, cid=999999999, service=999999 — byte-identical) |
| Q5 Novel | YES — no evidence of prior report |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES — not on the always-rejected list |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | YES — anonymous WS relay to backend CBS systems for any cid is a clear security finding |

**Verdict: VALID**

**Proof steps:** WS-upgrade GET `wss://cbs-proxy.api.live-manager.de/?origin=LiveDemo&cid=999999999&service=999999` with Upgrade/Connection/Sec-WebSocket headers (no auth); observe HTTP 101 + CONNECT + READY frames. Compare with `cid=1` — identical response. ~2 read-only requests, no data subscription.

**Impact:** Cross-tenant live call/debug stream attachment via anonymous WebSocket to internal CBS business systems. **HIGH** (broken access control on customer-facing proxy).

**CVSS 3.1:** `AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N` → **8.6 (High)**

**Reporting channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu — report + PoC + contact + payment

