### Finding 2: Static Credential Token Mint + Voicenote PII Leak (chained: `www.applicationdesigner.de` → `cbs-proxy`)

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 Scope | YES — `*.applicationdesigner.de` in scope |
| Q2 Reachable | YES — public help.js ships static credential; auth.php/voicenotes endpoints accept it unauthenticated |
| Q3 Impact | YES — anonymous per-cid debug token minting + real customer voicenote metadata (phone numbers, UUID filenames) exposed |
| Q4 Provable | YES — auth.php returns `success:true` for foreign cid=2; get.php/check.php return identical voicenote index ignoring customer_id |
| Q5 Novel | YES — static credential in public JS used as sole authorization across multiple endpoints |
| Q6 Not always-rejected | YES — not informational/benign; concrete PII disclosure + broken auth |
| Q7 Reasonable triager | YES — static credential that mints auth tokens for arbitrary tenants is a clear broken-auth bug |

**Verdict: VALID**

**Proof steps:** (1) GET `https://www.applicationdesigner.de/extjs/livedebugger/auth.php?token={sha256 8d2faac1...}&customer_id=2&srn=100` → `success:true` with auth hash. (2) GET `https://www.applicationdesigner.de/extjs/voicenotes/check.php?token={same}&customer_id=2` → `success:true total=1` (identical to cid=131727). Read-only, ~3 requests, no PII echoed in report.

**Impact:** Broken authentication allowing anonymous minting of per-tenant live-debug tokens for arbitrary customer IDs, combined with disclosure of real customer call/voicemail metadata (PII including phone numbers). **HIGH** (broken auth + PII exposure).

**CVSS 3.1:** `AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N` → **7.5 (High)**

**Reporting channel:** bugs.olivermaicher.eu

